ethercat (1.6.9+parallelop1~pre5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship udev rule (99-EtherCAT.rules) granting group "ethercat" access
    to /dev/EtherCAT* devices.
  * Create system group "ethercat" on install; remove on purge.
  * postinst prints reminder to add user to the ethercat group.
  * Rebased on Mika's dev-1.6 (FSM/EC_IO_TIMEOUT work, distro-tagged
    release artefacts).

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9+parallelop1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename binary package ethercat -> ethercat-master to match the
    OpenSUSE EtherLab naming convention. Provides/Replaces/Conflicts
    on ethercat for smooth upgrade.

 -- Luca Toniolo <toniolo.luca@gmail.com>  Mon, 27 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ethercat (1.6.9) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Parallel slave configuration (multi-slave bus reaches OP in seconds).
  * SDO information API and bus rescan in the realtime library.
  * Numerous stability fixes (datagram index reuse, external-ring timing,
    mailbox state machines, SDO dictionary gating, DC sync1 shift).
  * SII timing relaxed for slow EEPROMs.
  * New ethercat diag command, slave port bypass detection and upstream
    port inference.
  * FoE password support.

 -- mika <mika-net@outlook.com>  Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
